From: mi8 <mi8@local>
Subject: [PATCH] mi8-0177b: mark the window server debuggable from kern_exec

The first attempt patched sweet_amfi.c, but that patch never applied (the build log says
"bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c: patch does not apply" and skips it), so CS_DEBUGGED was never set
and dyld kept ignoring every DYLD_* variable for backboardd.

This does the same thing in a file whose patches do apply: kern_exec.c already collects
the image's code signing flags in imgp->ip_csflags and hands them to the process with
proc_csflags_update(). For the window server, CS_DEBUGGED is added there -- dyld takes
the process for one being debugged and honours DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES -- and a line is
printed so the log shows it happened.

--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exec.c
@@ -7357,8 +7357,20 @@
 	/*
 	 * Override inherited code signing flags with the
 	 * ones for the process that is being successfully
 	 * loaded
 	 */
+	/*
+	 * mi8 0177b: dyld refuses DYLD_* for a platform binary unless the process
+	 * looks debuggable, and this port marks every binary on the root
+	 * filesystem as a platform binary. The EAGL bridge has to get into the
+	 * window server, so that one program is marked debuggable here.
+	 */
+	if (strnstr(imgp->ip_strings, "usr/libexec/backboardd",
+	    strlen(EXECUTABLE_KEY) + MAXPATHLEN) != NULL &&
+	    (imgp->ip_csflags & CS_DEBUGGED) == 0) {
+		printf("sweet: backboardd is marked debuggable so dyld takes its DYLD_* variables\n");
+		imgp->ip_csflags |= CS_DEBUGGED;
+	}
 	proc_lock(p);
 	proc_csflags_update(p, imgp->ip_csflags);
 	proc_unlock(p);

